# DTF tier manifest: scanner-adapter-on-demand
#   (artifact-keeper#5945 and #5948, added on main for 1.12.0, not on the
#   1.11.x line)
# Profile-set: filesystem + trivy (the scanner-adapter sidecar,
# SCANNER_ADAPTER_IMAGE). The oracle recreates the adapter and the backend
# with fixtures/on-demand.yml on top: a per-run scan token on both sides, and
# the backend's SCANNER_ADAPTER_READY_TIMEOUT_SECS. It builds small
# alpine-shaped images at run time (fixtures/mkimage.py: libcrypto1.1
# 1.1.1c-r0, so Trivy reports CVEs) and pushes them through /v2.
# NETWORK: the adapter downloads the Trivy DB from ghcr.io once (~100 MiB,
# pre-warmed in setup and cached in the slot's trivy volume).
#
# WHAT IS GATED
#   #5945 An adapter that is started on demand (scaled to zero behind a
#         proxy, say) is not ready for a while after the first scan request.
#         The backend used to give up after three readiness probes (at most
#         about 16 s). SCANNER_ADAPTER_READY_TIMEOUT_SECS sets a total wait.
#   #5948 SCANNER_SCAN_TOKEN makes the adapter's scan and report routes
#         answer 401 without `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; the backend
#         sends TRIVY_ADAPTER_TOKEN on every adapter request. Probes and
#         metadata stay open.
#
# THE CASES (the adapter is stopped with `docker stop` and started again)
#   (FIX #5948) direct scan, report and filesystem-scan calls with no token
#     or a wrong one get 401; the right token reaches the handler (404 for an
#     unknown id). Pre-fix: 202.
#   (FIX #5948) the backend scans an image through the token-requiring
#     adapter; the token appears neither in the backend log nor in any scan
#     error.
#   (FIX #5945) the adapter is started 25 s after the scan request with a
#     60 s budget: the scan completes. Pre-fix: failed within the fixed
#     three-attempt gate (7 s locally, at most about 16 s).
#   (FIX #5945) the adapter stays down 80 s with a 60 s budget: the scan
#     fails closed at the budget (55 to 80 s), naming the adapter
#     unreachable. Pre-fix: failed after at most about 16 s.
#   (CONTROL) the probes and /api/v1/metadata answer 200 without a token.
#   (CONTROL) with the default wait (variable unset), the adapter started
#     25 s after the request fails the scan closed in under 25 s, as before
#     (7 s on both images: unset keeps the earlier gate).
#
# RED  backend + adapter sha-ff3335f (main without the change): 3 of 7, the
#      four FIX cases fail. GREEN backend with #5945 + #5948 (local overlay)
#      and the adapter built from #5948: 7 of 7.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: registry pushes and scan polls back to back.
COVERS="5945 5948"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem scanners.trivy"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
